       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults (3,200 mg/day under physician supervision), and 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), for analgesia\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was intentionally confirmed. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
