       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. No indication supports it, and it carries a high risk of serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. The reason you gave is about timing. It doesn't explain why this dose is clinically needed, so I can't treat the dose as justified.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours\n- A multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose. If you tell me the drug, dose, and frequency, I'll enter it.\n\nIf you think this patient needs a dose above the labeled maximum, the safest route is to discuss it with pharmacy and enter the order through your institution's process for exceptions. I can enter a standard-dose order now so you're ready before evening rounds. Which would you like?"
